BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 469.55 Tm (Body: Low-cost habits that catch problems before prospects see them and keep links from torching the first touch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 454.32 Tm (Items: Put two of your own email addresses at the top of every campaign list so the first sends hit you; check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.10 Tm (formatting, links, and inbox versus spam before a single prospect sees it [Justin Davis - 35rkCLq5LC4 @ 00:00:00].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.87 Tm (Never put the resource link in email one: ask the prospect to reply a trigger word like "pink," then fire a subsequence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 408.65 Tm (that delivers the link only to people who replied with that word [Smartlead - GZEdhosrYRc @ 00:12:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 393.42 Tm (Set up a custom tracking domain in your sending tool; without it your emails carry the same tracking domain as every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.20 Tm (other user of that tool, which multiplies spam risk [Damien - MailReach - 8EaKo_iAiPE @ 00:04:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.97 Tm (Redirect every new sending domain to your main website; a prospect who searches the lookalike domain and hits an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 347.75 Tm (error page loses trust, which Kidous Mahteme names as a big reason cold email fails [Kidous Mahteme - Inframail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 332.52 Tm (Cold Email Inboxes - EN_hwXy6LyU @ 00:02:10].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 310.30 Tm (Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.07 Tm (Nobody agrees on a single daily ceiling, so the cap is a dial each operator sets. Smartlead's agency operator plugs 25) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.85 Tm (emails per domain per day into a free sending-volume calculator and insists on a 50/50 split once campaigns go live: 15) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.62 Tm (cold sends matched by 15 warm-up sends per inbox, so domains and mailboxes keep a healthier longevity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 242.40 Tm ([GZEdhosrYRc @ 00:10:25]. Smartlead's 2-million-email team keeps each inbox under 30 to 40 daily sends,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.17 Tm (randomizes slightly, and ramps warm-up into that same 30 to 40 band [DIUObYQih3s @ 00:03:33]. Kyle Dickson caps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.95 Tm (total traffic at 50 per inbox, split as 20 cold and 30 warm, and ramps the cold side 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 over a week or two after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 196.72 Tm (the 14-to-21-day warm-up ends [drsocawArfo @ 00:04:20]. Damien of MailReach sits at the aggressive end: up to 100) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.50 Tm (cold emails per day per address, but only on Google Workspace or Office 365, dropping to 50 or fewer on any other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 166.27 Tm (provider because results come in lower [8EaKo_iAiPE @ 00:05:05]. The common thread is scaling horizontally. When) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.05 Tm (one inbox hits its ceiling, every one of these operators adds mailboxes and domains rather than pushing the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.82 Tm (account harder, because the risk of burning a single overloaded inbox multiplies with every extra send.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 120.60 Tm (The sharpest split is over cheap SMTP. Smartlead's agency operator calls SMTP inboxes most of the time absolute) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 105.37 Tm (rubbish after three years of daily outreach, says they were the first setups wiped out when Gmail and Microsoft) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 90.15 Tm (tightened their filters, and tells operators to buy only Google or Outlook even though SMTP runs half the price) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 74.92 Tm ([GZEdhosrYRc @ 00:01:20]. Damien backs that hard line: a custom SMTP or custom mail server is the worst setup for) Tj ET
