BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.55 Tm (The most expensive failure the operators report is torching the main domain. The Smartlead agency operator has taken) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.32 Tm (on clients whose entire email communication was compromised after outreach ran off the primary domain, because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.10 Tm (spam marks follow every email that domain sends, including mail to existing clients, vendors and providers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.87 Tm ([dTLQCIO7Tf0 @ 00:01:28]. The Reachflow walkthrough describes the same wreck: clients whose internal emails) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.65 Tm (land in spam after thousands of cold sends without best practices got the domain blacklisted [_lMStnTXkVM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.42 Tm (00:03:14]. Even clean secondary infrastructure wears out. The Smartlead operator says mailboxes will burn and need) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.20 Tm (replacing, so anyone sending from five domains and 10 mailboxes should keep another five domains and 10 mailboxes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 236.97 Tm (warming as backup, and the agency pulled mailboxes from its own infrastructure after a weekend spam-placement test) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.75 Tm ([dTLQCIO7Tf0 @ 00:15:06]. Provider mix is the quieter leak: Reachflow contacts Google Workspace leads first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.52 Tm (SMTP leads second and Microsoft leads last because Microsoft deliverability is not comparable, and it switches off) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.30 Tm (open and link-click tracking [_lMStnTXkVM @ 00:08:57]. The economics check is blunt. Reachflow ties better copy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.07 Tm (to fewer spam marks, which keeps the current mailboxes alive longer and saves the money that replacement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.85 Tm (infrastructure would otherwise eat.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.62 Tm (Early-stage operators kill campaigns before the data means anything. Gardiner watches beginners email 100 or 200) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.40 Tm (people, get disheartened and quit, so the floor is at least 500 contacts plus a day or two of waiting for late replies before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.17 Tm (touching the copy [A58LBIib2rc @ 00:06:31]. The Smartlead operator sets the bar far higher: the first two or three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 99.95 Tm (campaigns are learning campaigns, and no copy change happens before 2,000 contacts [dTLQCIO7Tf0 @ 00:13:34].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 84.72 Tm (Gardiner also names the agency-owner trap of acting like a CEO who hires out all fulfillment, which is how people fail,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 69.50 Tm (because the owner has to write the instruction manuals and step back in when hires quit, get sick or end up sucking) Tj ET
