BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Kind: OPERATOR GATE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Title: Four traps to block before the first campaign goes live) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Body: Each of these is a pitfall the operators hit themselves or cleaned up for clients, and each is cheaper to block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (before launch than to repair after a domain is reported.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Items: No cold send leaves the primary domain; outreach runs only on secondary domains redirected to the main site,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (because spam marks carry over to client and vendor mail [Smartlead - dTLQCIO7Tf0 @ 00:01:08].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (Every opt-out lands on a global block list before any lead list gets deleted, and that contact is never emailed again) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (unless they reach out first [Namit Jindal | Aerosend - OhSoUY7K_dU @ 00:05:30].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Every message carries a real physical address in the footer, first touch included, so the email never reads as a phantom) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (sender hiding behind a domain [Cold Pipeline - tfCx05hBH78 @ 00:03:23].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Suppression is centralized across every rep and sending account so an opt-out from one sender cannot be emailed by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (another two weeks later [Misar AI - gz6GYKesDk4 @ 00:17:53].) Tj ET
BT /F0 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (Pull Quote) Tj ET
